{
  "id": "leetcode-36",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "approved",
  "title": "Valid Sudoku",
  "summary": "Determine if a 9 x 9 Sudoku board is valid by ensuring that each row, column, and 3 x 3 sub-box contains the digits 1-9 without any repetitions.",
  "statement": "Determine if a 9 x 9 Sudoku board is valid by ensuring that each row, column, and 3 x 3 sub-box contains the digits 1-9 without any repetitions. Focus solely on the filled cells to validate according to the specified rules.",
  "constraints": [
    "The board is exactly 9×9. Each cell is '.', meaning empty, or a digit character from '1' through '9'.",
    "Validate only the filled cells: no repeated digit in any row, column, or aligned 3×3 box. Empty cells may repeat freely. Do not fill the board or require that a completion exists."
  ],
  "topics": [
    "matrices",
    "hash-maps"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [],
  "signature": {
    "name": "valid_sudoku",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "board",
        "annotation": "list[list[str]]",
        "adapter": "raw",
        "source_parameter": null
      }
    ],
    "returns": "bool",
    "return_adapter": "raw",
    "node_policy": "values",
    "result_mode": "return",
    "mutated_parameter": null,
    "immutable_parameters": []
  },
  "starter_code": "def valid_sudoku(board: list[list[str]]) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n",
  "reference_solution": "def valid_sudoku(board):\n    rows = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    columns = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    boxes = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    for row in range(9):\n        for column in range(9):\n            digit = board[row][column]\n            if digit == \".\":\n                continue\n            box = row // 3 * 3 + column // 3\n            if digit in rows[row] or digit in columns[column] or digit in boxes[box]:\n                return False\n            rows[row].add(digit)\n            columns[column].add(digit)\n            boxes[box].add(digit)\n    return True\n",
  "brute_force_solution": null,
  "known_wrong_solutions": [
    "def valid_sudoku(board):\n    rows = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    columns = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    boxes = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    for row in range(9):\n        for column in range(9):\n            digit = board[row][column]\n            if digit == \".\":\n                continue\n            box = row // 3 * 3 + column // 3\n            if digit in rows[row] or digit in columns[column]:\n                return False\n            rows[row].add(digit)\n            columns[column].add(digit)\n            boxes[box].add(digit)\n    return True\n",
    "def valid_sudoku(board):\n    rows = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    columns = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    boxes = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    for row in range(9):\n        for column in range(9):\n            digit = board[row][column]\n            if False:\n                continue\n            box = row // 3 * 3 + column // 3\n            if digit in rows[row] or digit in columns[column] or digit in boxes[box]:\n                return False\n            rows[row].add(digit)\n            columns[column].add(digit)\n            boxes[box].add(digit)\n    return True\n"
  ],
  "target_time_complexity": "O(81), constant for a 9×9 board",
  "target_space_complexity": "O(81), constant for a 9×9 board",
  "estimated_minutes": 35,
  "rubric": {
    "algorithmic_insight": 2,
    "prerequisites": 1,
    "implementation": 1,
    "performance_pressure": 1,
    "edge_cases": 0
  },
  "hints": [
    "This checks consistency of filled cells, not whether you can solve the puzzle.",
    "Track seen digits independently for each row, each column, and each 3×3 box.",
    "Skip dots. Compute box=(row//3)*3+column//3, reject an already-seen digit in any of its three sets, then add it to all three.",
    "Two matching digits can share a box without sharing a row or column; all three checks are necessary."
  ],
  "editorial": "Scan the 81 cells and maintain three groups of nine sets. A duplicate in any relevant unit violates Sudoku's rules; otherwise the partial board is valid, even if a blank cell cannot later be filled. A deliberate valid-but-unsolvable fixture guards that distinction. The independent oracle compares pairs of filled cells and checks whether matching digits share a row, column, or box instead of maintaining unit sets. Time and storage are constant for the fixed 9×9 domain.",
